    description "Making a first knife can be intimidating.  But blade smith Walter Sorrells leads you through the making of simple but excellent knife using nothing but simple hand tools.  (Okay...and a kitchen oven.)   The video also demonstrates a small, cheap heat treating forge.  The build for that forge is shown in another video that can be found here:  https://youtu.be/iwX_lf4WwBc&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Buy the actual knife made in this video at:   http://www.tactixarmory.com/specials&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Check out Walter's videos about making Japanese swords:  http://www.waltersorrellsblades.com&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Support the channel on Patreon:  http://www.patreon.com/WalterSorrells&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Tactix Armory knives:  http://www.tactixarmory.com&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Walter's Instagram:  walterstactix&amp;#10;Tactix Armory Instagram:  tactixarmory&amp;#10;Twitter:  @WalterSorrells&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Help the channel and get a discount on belts from Combat Abrasives! https://www.combatabrasives.com/discount/blade1?rfsn=2862769.5fbedb7&amp;#38;utm_source=refersion&amp;#38;subid=YoutubeFF48"
