    step 0
    date "2020-09-26T11:26:51Z"
    title "Top 10 Power Tools for Beginner Woodworkers"
    description "What power tools do you need to start woodworking or to setup your first workshop?  It can be difficult to know where to start, so Scott walks you through his recommendation of what tools to buy.  This video was inspired by John Malecki's video for must-have tools ( https://youtu.be/2eFeB2fTiQ ).  &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Here's a list of power tools to start with:&amp;#10;- Random Orbital Sander&amp;#10;- Shop Vacuum with a HEPA filter&amp;#10;- Drill and countersink pilot hole bit&amp;#10;- Circular Saw for cutting straight lines&amp;#10;- Jigsaw for cutting curved lines and circles&amp;#10;&amp;#10;If you're setting up your first workshop (an exciting time!), here are the recommended power tools to buy:&amp;#10;- Miter Saw&amp;#10;- Table Saw&amp;#10;- Dust Collector&amp;#10;- Router&amp;#10;- Drill Press&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Here's a link to Made for Profit Podcast, where John and Brad offer great advice to the Maker community - https://madeforprofit.com&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Our woodworking plans - https://woodenitbenice.ca/collections/woodworking-plans&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Our 1-on-1 woodworking advice sessions -  https://woodenitbenice.ca/collections/woodworking-advice-sessions&amp;#10;&amp;#10;See the tools we use in our workshop and the tools we recommend: https://www.amazon.com/shop/homeimprovementwoodworking&amp;#10;&amp;#127464;&amp;#127462; Canadian link - https://www.amazon.ca/shop/homeimprovementwoodworking&amp;#10;&amp;#10;For more woodworking knowledge or to contact us directly, visit our website   https://WoodenItBeNice.ca  Hosted by Scott Bennett, owner of Wooden It Be Nice in Brooklin, Ontario, Canada"
    channeltitle "Home Improvement Woodworking"
